Subject: [PATCH 16/28] fix(midea): correct the carpet avoidance bit 3 quirk
 description

Bit 3 of the 0x5E carpet settings is stored by the firmware as
carpet-setting-ai-aviod, i.e. camera/AI carpet detection feeding the
avoidance map, not a larger distance margin to carpets.

Retitle the quirk and fix its description. The id and the bit handling
are unchanged.

Based on static analysis; untested. The key name is confirmed, the exact
behaviour is likely.

diff --git a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js
index c05c7172..8f5490e3 100644
--- a/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js
+++ b/backend/lib/robots/midea/MideaQuirkFactory.js
@@ -379,8 +379,8 @@ class MideaQuirkFactory {
             case MideaQuirkFactory.KNOWN_QUIRKS.INCREASED_CARPET_AVOIDANCE:
                 return new Quirk({
                     id: id,
-                    title: "Increased Carpet Avoidance",
-                    description: "When enabled, when avoiding carpets, the robot will stay further away from them.",
+                    title: "AI Carpet Detection",
+                    description: "When enabled, carpets detected by the camera are added to the carpet avoidance map in addition to the ones recorded by the carpet sensor.",
                     options: ["off", "on"],
